{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 15,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should a wise men utter vain knowledge, and fill his belly with the east wind?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should he reason with unprofitable talk? or with speeches with which he can do no good?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, thou castest off fear, and restrainest prayer before God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thy mouth uttereth thy iniquity, and thou choosest the tongue of the crafty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy own mouth condemneth thee, and not I: yes, thy own lips testify against thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou the first man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " was born? or wast thou made before the hills?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou heard the secret of God? and dost thou restrain wisdom to thyself?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What knowest thou that we know not? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "what",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " understandest thou, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not in us?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With us ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " both the gray headed and very aged men, much older than thy father.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the consolations of God small with thee? is there any secret thing with thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why doth thy heart carry thee away? and what do thy eyes wink at,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That thou turnest thy spirit against God, and lettest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "such",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " words go out of thy mouth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man, that he should be clean? and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he who is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " born of a woman, that he should be righteous?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he putteth no trust in his saints; yes, the heavens are not clean in his sight.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much more abominable and filthy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man, who drinketh iniquity like water?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will show thee, hear me; and that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I have seen, I will declare;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which wise men have told from their fathers, and have not hid ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ":",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom alone the earth was given, and no stranger passed among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked man travaileth with pain all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " days, and the number of years is hidden to the oppressor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A dreadful sound ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his ears: in prosperity the destroyer shall come upon him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He believeth not that he shall return out of darkness, and he is waited for by the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He wandereth abroad for bread, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? he knoweth that the day of darkness is ready at his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Trouble and anguish shall make him afraid; they shall prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he stretcheth out his hand against God, and strengtheneth himself against the Almighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He runneth upon him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " neck, upon the thick bosses of his bucklers:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because he covereth his face with his fatness, and maketh collops of fat on ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " flanks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he dwelleth in desolate cities, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in houses which no man inhabiteth, which are ready to become heaps.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall not be rich, neither shall his substance continue, neither shall he prolong the perfection of it upon the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall not depart out of darkness; the flame shall dry up his branches, and by the breath of his mouth shall he go away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not him that is deceived trust in vanity: for vanity shall be his recompense.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It shall be accomplished before his time, and his branch shall not be green.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall shake off his unripe grape as the vine, and shall cast off his flower as the olive.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the congregation of hypocrites ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " desolate, and fire shall consume the tabernacles of bribery.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.15.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They conceive mischief, and bring forth vanity, and their belly prepareth deceit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
